# K816's own linked bytes, compared by tests/compat.rs.
#
# 2000  A9 01        LDA #$01      far_one
# 2002  6B           RTL           a far section returns long
# 2003  A9 02        LDA #$02      near_one
# 2005  60           RTS
# 2006  A9 34 12     LDA #$1234    wide, assembled @a16
# 2009  60           RTS
# 200A  22 00 20 00  JSL $002000   call far far_one   - long call, long return
# 200E  20 03 20     JSR $2003     call near_one      - short call, short return
# 2011  C2 20        REP #$20      the bridge to wide's entry contract
# 2013  20 06 20     JSR $2006     call wide
# 2016  60           RTS
#
# Lowering emits `rep #$20` *and* `rep #$10` for that bridge; the optimizer
# drops the index half because nothing in `wide` observes the index width.
# That is F's business (`optimizer-dead-register-write`), not this row's, and
# it is here so a change to it is noticed.

origin 2000
2000  A9 01 6B A9 02 60 A9 34 12 60 22 00 20 00 20 03
2010  20 C2 20 20 06 20 60
